+### 13.6a Native workflow supply receiving (CC-RS-WR-SUPPLY-FIT)
+
+This bounded technical revision adds `incomparable` and a native coordinate to
+R3 workflow start/end-notice forms only. It preserves RS format 0.1 and the
+existing positive-integer `turn` namespace. For these forms exactly one of
+`turn` or `nativeTurn` is present. `nativeTurn` is the opaque supplier turn
+identity paired with nonempty `thread`; it is never parsed, hashed, counted,
+or equated to an ordinal. Historical numeric records retain their bytes and
+meaning. No numeric producer or mapping is established by this change.
+
+The native form requires `supplyCheckRecord`, `supplyRecord`, `supplyCheck` and
+`adoption: "unknown"`. A native receiving operation resolves both WR references
+in the explicitly opened owning project through WR's immutable publication
+resolver. Both references are evidence kind `supply record`; each ref is
+`wr-record:v1:<lower-case UUID>` and each `resolutionAtWrite` records its actual
+resolution. New native R3 publication requires both to resolve. JSON shape
+validation is a prerequisite, never evidence that native supply occurred.
+
+Publishing run_text before send establishes preparation only. A queued or failed
+send, client message ID, or written frame alone does not establish supplied
+text or a native turn. Until source-bound native turn and actual send/check
+evidence exist, retain the prepared record and report R3 pending/unavailable;
+never manufacture nativeTurn from client_user_message_id.
+
+The receiving operation verifies the RS runId, thread, purpose and composed
+text method/value against the resolved WR run_text and supply_check; maps
+purpose exactly to start/end-notice supplyForm; preserves the workflow's full
+source identity through run_text; and requires nativeTurn equal the exact
+WR check.turn. A known native request turn remains that coordinate even when
+its check is not found/unreadable; if no source-bound turn is available,
+retain WR evidence and report R3 unavailable rather than invent a coordinate.
+The RS content is the composed text identity, not the workflow package digest.
+Client message/item/source-receipt references stay in WR's evidence account;
+RS does not copy a native transcript, generated prompt, or WR body.
+
+Copy WR's state exactly, including incomparable. Incomparable reads
+"supplied — not verified, incomparable methods"; it is neither mismatch,
+unreadable nor not checked. Equal value strings under different methods do
+not establish equality. All other non-verified states remain supplied — not
+verified; verified establishes supply only. Adoption stays unknown.
+
+On later reads an unresolved or conflicting reference produces an explicit
+reference/evidence limit; retain the recorded observation without upgrading
+its standing. Deserializing a historical claim or source receipt does not
+recreate live native-owner witness authority. Rereading native history creates
+a new WR check and a new R3 observation; retrying the publication of the same
+pending check preserves that check's identity and does not resend the turn.
+
+This is an in-place proposed-schema revision, as earlier format-0.1 changes,
+not forward compatibility. Design and bundled consumers must adopt the exact
+reviewed schema together before emitting nativeTurn/incomparable. An older
+strict reader rejects these records as unsupported/invalid with an incomplete
+record limit, retaining original bytes; it must not remove fields or relabel
+states. No automatic migration, inferred ordinal, model_turn or EXEC change
+is authorized. VC-40 additionally covers native start/end notice, every WR
+state, immutable reference joins, cold resolution and refusal of guessed
+coordinates or mismatched source/run/thread/purpose/text identities.
+
